ENTRY 9445 {"id":9445,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"# pi-durable-k8s\n\nRun [Pi Durable](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi) coding agents on your own Kubernetes cluster.\n\nEach session gets an agent that keeps its state in PostgreSQL and resumes after a crash, plus a private gVisor\nsandbox with a persistent workspace where its tools run. Model and GitHub credentials never reach the agent or the\nsandbox: [OneCLI](https://github.com/onecli/onecli) injects them at its gateway.\n\n**Status: proof of concept.** It runs end to end on a small arm64 lab cluster. It is not hardened for production;\nsee the open items in [plan.md](plan.md).\n\n![Architecture](docs/architecture.svg)\n\n## How it works\n\n1. A client creates a session and posts messages to the **session API** (`packages/ingest`).\n2. Messages land in an inbox in **PostgreSQL** first, so nothing is lost while the agent is busy or restarting.\n3. The **orchestrator** (`packages/orchestrator`) runs one durable Pi agent loop per session and takes inbox\n   messages in order.\n4. Model calls go through the **OneCLI gateway**, which adds the subscription or API key on the way out.\n5. Tool calls (bash, read, write, edit) run in the session's **sandbox**: a pod from\n   [agent-sandbox](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/agent-sandbox) under gVisor, with the `pi-env` daemon inside.\n   It is created on the first tool call and keeps its workspace on a PVC.\n6. Progress and answers stream back to the client over SSE.\n\nOptionally a session works on one GitHub repository: the orchestrator mints a token scoped to that repository,\nstores it in OneCLI for that session only, and the sandbox clones and pushes through the gateway.\n\n## Security model\n\n- Sandboxes run under gVisor. Network policies (written for Cilium) block sandboxes from the orchestrator, the\n  database, the Kubernetes API, OneCLI's management API and each other.\n- Each sandbox's daemon accepts only its own token, derived from a master key the orchestrator holds\n  ([ADR 0001](docs/decisions/0001-per-sandbox-sandboxd-token.md)).\n- No credentials in sandboxes or in the agent: OneCLI holds them and only relays to allowlisted hosts\n  ([host rules](docs/onecli-host-rules.md)).\n\n## Repository layout\n\n| Path                                   | What                                                                                                 |\n| -------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `packages/ingest`                      | Session API: auth, owner checks, inbox writes, SSE proxy                                             |\n| `packages/orchestrator`                | Pi Durable harness, sandbox lifecycle, model and OneCLI wiring                                       |\n| `packages/sandbox-env`                 | Bridge from Pi's `RemoteExecutionEnv` to an agent-sandbox pod (the only SDK user)                    |\n| `packages/session-core`                | Shared schema, migrations and auth helpers                                                           |\n| `packages/vendor/agent-sandbox-client` | Vendored, pinned agent-sandbox TypeScript SDK (Apache-2.0)                                           |\n| `vendor/`                              | Packed `@netzlabor/pi-durable-postgres` adapter, ported to Pi Durable 1.5.2                          |\n| `images/sandbox`                       | Sandbox image: sandboxd + `pi-env` + git                                                             |\n| `deploy/`                              | Kubernetes manifests (namespace, Postgres, orchestrator, ingest, sandbox template, network policies) |\n| `tests/e2e`                            | End-to-end suites that run as in-cluster Jobs                                                        |\n| `docs/`                                | API, credentials, networking, decisions and research notes                                           |\n\n## Docs\n\n- [Session API](docs/session-api.md)\n- [Model credentials through OneCLI](docs/model-credentials.md)\n- [Repository workspaces](docs/repo-workspace.md)\n- [Network policy](docs/network-policy.md) and [OneCLI host rules](docs/onecli-host-rules.md)\n- [Plan, decisions and phase results](plan.md)\n\n## Development\n\nRequires Node 22.19+ and pnpm.\n\n```sh\npnpm install\npnpm check        # build, lint, format, typecheck, unit tests\ntests/e2e/run.sh smoke   # needs a cluster with agent-sandbox, gVisor and the deploy/ manifests applied\n```\n\n## License\n\nMIT, see [LICENSE](LICENSE). The vendored agent-sandbox SDK in `packages/vendor/agent-sandbox-client` keeps its Apache-2.0 license.\n  193 packages/orchestrator/src/inbox.ts\n  304 packages/orchestrator/src/host.ts\n   90 packages/orchestrator/src/watcher.ts\n  193 packages/orchestrator/src/stream.ts\n  168 packages/orchestrator/src/main.ts\n   34 packages/orchestrator/src/failure.ts\n  345 packages/session-core/src/store.ts\n 1327 total\n","isError":false}]}
ENTRY 9449 {"id":9449,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"","calls":["bash({\"command\":\"cd /workspace/repo && for f in packages/orchestrator/src/{inbox,host,watcher,stream,main,failure}.ts packages/session-core/src/store.ts; do echo ==== $f; nl -ba \\\"$f\\\"; done\",\"timeout\":10000})"]}]}
ENTRY 9455 {"id":9455,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"     4\timport type {\n     5\t  Conversation,\n     6\t  ConversationId,\n     7\t  ConversationWatch,\n     8\t  ConversationWindow,\n     9\t  Cursor,\n    10\t  Storage,\n    11\t} from \"@earendil-works/pi-durable\";\n    12\timport type { ModelChoice } from \"@pi-durable-k8s/session-core\";\n    13\timport { createCodingTools } from \"@earendil-works/pi-durable/tools\";\n    14\timport type { OrchestratorConfig } from \"./config.js\";\n    15\timport { errorMessage, log } from \"./log.js\";\n    16\timport type { Script } from \"./model.js\";\n    17\timport { buildModels } from \"./providers.js\";\n    18\timport { claimNameFor, Sandboxes, WORKSPACE } from \"./sandboxes.js\";\n    19\timport type { SandboxHooks, SessionKeyOf } from \"./sandboxes.js\";\n    20\timport type { SubmissionState } from \"./watcher.js\";\n    21\timport type { WorkspaceEnv } from \"./workspace.js\";\n    22\t\n    23\texport interface SessionEvent {\n    24\t  role: Message[\"role\"];\n    25\t  /** Assistant text, tool output, or the user's script. */\n    26\t  text: string;\n    27\t  /** Tool calls the assistant made, as `name(args)`. */\n    28\t  calls?: string[];\n    29\t  /** Tool results only. */\n    30\t  isError?: boolean;\n    31\t}\n    32\t\n    33\texport interface SessionStatus {\n    34\t  id: number;\n    35\t  claim: string;\n    36\t  state: \"running\" | \"done\";\n    37\t  events: number;\n    38\t  /** Text of every tool result so far, in order. */\n    39\t  results: { text: string; isError: boolean }[];\n    40\t  answer?: string;\n    41\t}\n    42\t\n    43\tfunction contentText(content: Message[\"content\"]): string {\n    44\t  if (typeof content === \"string\") return content;\n    45\t  return content\n    46\t    .map((block) => {\n    47\t      if (block.type === \"text\") return block.text;\n    48\t      return block.type === \"toolCall\" ? \"\" : `[${block.type}]`;\n    49\t    })\n    50\t    .join(\"\");\n    51\t}\n    52\t\n    53\texport function toEvent(message: Message): SessionEvent {\n    54\t  const event: SessionEvent = { role: message.role, text: contentText(message.content) };\n    55\t  if (message.role === \"assistant\") {\n    56\t    const calls = message.content.flatMap((block) =>\n    57\t      block.type === \"toolCall\" ? [`${block.name}(${JSON.stringify(block.arguments)})`] : [],\n    58\t    );\n    59\t    if (calls.length > 0) event.calls = calls;\n    60\t  }\n    61\t  if (message.role === \"toolResult\") event.isError = message.isError;\n    62\t  return event;\n    63\t}\n    64\t\n    65\t/** The Pi Durable host: one Harness over the Postgres storage, one conversation per session. */\n    66\texport class Host {\n    67\t  readonly #harness: Harness;\n    68\t  readonly #sandboxes: Sandboxes;\n    69\t  readonly #storage: Storage;\n    70\t\n    71\t  private constructor(harness: Harness, sandboxes: Sandboxes, storage: Storage) {\n    72\t    this.#harness = harness;\n    73\t    this.#sandboxes = sandboxes;\n    74\t    this.#storage = storage;\n    75\t  }\n    76\t\n    77\t  /**\n    78\t   * Opens the Harness over an owned storage and resumes whatever the last process left running.\n    79\t   * `onFailed` fires when the Harness ends on a storage error, e.g. the database connection died.\n    80\t   */\n    81\t  static async open(\n    82\t    storage: Storage,\n    83\t    config: OrchestratorConfig,\n    84\t    onFailed: (error: unknown) => void,\n    85\t    sessionKeyOf: SessionKeyOf,\n    86\t    hooks: SandboxHooks = {},\n    87\t    recycleAtStart: readonly number[] = [],\n    88\t  ): Promise<Host> {\n    89\t    const models = await buildModels(config);\n    90\t    const registry = createRegistry();\n    91\t    registry.install(createCodingTools());\n    92\t    const sandboxes = new Sandboxes(config, sessionKeyOf, hooks);\n    93\t    // Before resume(): a continuing run must not run its next command in a Pod that still holds the leftovers of\n    94\t    // the command the previous process was killed in.\n    95\t    sandboxes.recycleAtStart(recycleAtStart);\n    96\t\n    97\t    const harness = await Harness.open(\n    98\t      storage,\n    99\t      {\n   100\t        models,\n   101\t        registry,\n   102\t        // Lazy: the SandboxClaim is created at the first tool call, not at the first model request.\n   103\t        env: ({ conversationId }) => Promise.resolve(sandboxes.lazyEnv(Number(conversationId))),\n   104\t        onReport: (report) => {\n   105\t          log(\"report\", { kind: report.kind, message: errorMessage(report.error) });\n   106\t        },\n   107\t      },\n   108\t      context,\n   109\t    );\n   110\t    void harness.closed.then((end) => {\n   111\t      if (end.kind === \"failed\") onFailed(end.error);\n   112\t    });\n   113\t    // No new input needed: open recovers nothing by itself, resume() continues unfinished runs.\n   114\t    harness.resume();\n   115\t    return new Host(harness, sandboxes, storage);\n   116\t  }\n   117\t\n   118\t  /** Creates the conversation and its sandbox claim, then submits the script as the first input. */\n   119\t  async startSession(script: Script): Promise<{ id: number; claim: string }> {\n   120\t    const conversation = await this.#harness.createConversation(\n   121\t      {\n   122\t        ownership: { kind: \"ownerless\" },\n   123\t        agent: { model: { provider: \"faux\", modelId: \"faux-1\" }, cwd: WORKSPACE },\n   124\t      },\n   125\t      context,\n   126\t    );\n   127\t    const id = Number(conversation.id);\n   128\t    await this.#sandboxes.ensure(id);\n   129\t    await conversation.submit(\n   130\t      { type: \"input\", content: JSON.stringify(script), requestId: `start-${String(id)}` },\n   131\t      context,\n   132\t    );\n   133\t    log(\"session-started\", { id, claim: claimNameFor(id) });\n   134\t    return { id, claim: claimNameFor(id) };\n   135\t  }\n   136\t\n   137\t  /** A further input to an existing session; the model follows the newest script. False if unknown. */\n   138\t  async sendInput(id: number, script: Script): Promise<boolean> {\n   139\t    const conversation = await this.#harness.conversation(id as ConversationId, context);\n   140\t    if (conversation === undefined) return false;\n   141\t    await conversation.submit({ type: \"input\", content: JSON.stringify(script) }, context);\n   142\t    return true;\n   143\t  }\n   144\t\n   145\t  async events(id: number): Promise<SessionEvent[] | undefined> {\n   146\t    const conversation = await this.#harness.conversation(id as ConversationId, context);\n   147\t    if (conversation === undefined) return undefined;\n   148\t    const view = await conversation.context(context);\n   149\t    // Stored entries, not view.messages: the view adds a placeholder result for a call still running.\n   150\t    return view.entries.flatMap((entry) => entry.model ?? []).map(toEvent);\n   151\t  }\n   152\t\n   153\t  async status(id: number): Promise<SessionStatus | undefined> {\n   154\t    const events = await this.events(id);\n   155\t    if (events === undefined) return undefined;\n   156\t    const last = events.at(-1);\n   157\t    const results = events\n   158\t      .filter((e) => e.role === \"toolResult\")\n   159\t      .map((e) => ({ text: e.text, isError: e.isError === true }));\n   160\t    const answered = last?.role === \"assistant\" && last.calls === undefined;\n   161\t    return {\n   162\t      id,\n   163\t      claim: claimNameFor(id),\n   164\t      state: answered ? \"done\" : \"running\",\n   165\t      events: events.length,\n   166\t      results,\n   167\t      ...(answered ? { answer: last.text } : {}),\n   168\t    };\n   169\t  }\n   170\t\n   171\t  /**\n   172\t   * Creates an empty conversation for a session, running on `model`. No sandbox: that is created lazily, at the\n   173\t   * first tool call, by the `env` callback of the Harness.\n   174\t   *\n   175\t   * Pi Durable stores the model in the conversation's `pi.agent` document, in the creating commit. It survives\n   176\t   * restarts, so it is set once here and not on every turn; only the provider must be installed again at each start.\n   177\t   */\n   178\t  async createConversation(model: ModelChoice): Promise<number> {\n   179\t    const conversation = await this.#harness.createConversation(\n   180\t      {\n   181\t        ownership: { kind: \"ownerless\" },\n   182\t        agent: {\n   183\t          model: { provider: model.provider, modelId: model.model },\n   184\t          ...(model.reasoning === undefined ? {} : { thinkingLevel: model.reasoning }),\n   185\t          cwd: WORKSPACE,\n   186\t        },\n   187\t      },\n   188\t      context,\n   189\t    );\n   190\t    return Number(conversation.id);\n   191\t  }\n   192\t\n   193\t  /** The model a conversation runs on, as Pi Durable stored it. */\n   194\t  async modelOf(id: number): Promise<ModelChoice | undefined> {\n   195\t    const agent = await (await this.#conversation(id)).agent(context);\n   196\t    return agent.model === undefined\n   197\t      ? undefined\n   198\t      : { provider: agent.model.provider, model: agent.model.modelId };\n   199\t  }\n   200\t\n   201\t  /** The reasoning effort a conversation runs with, as Pi Durable resolved it (`off` when none was stored). */\n   202\t  async thinkingOf(id: number): Promise<string> {\n   203\t    return (await (await this.#conversation(id)).agent(context)).thinkingLevel;\n   204\t  }\n   205\t\n   206\t  /** Model turns (assistant responses) in the conversation's transcript so far. */\n   207\t  async turnsUsed(id: number): Promise<number> {\n   208\t    const conversation = await this.#conversation(id);\n   209\t    let turns = 0;\n   210\t    let cursor: Cursor | undefined;\n   211\t    do {\n   212\t      const page = await conversation.entries({ order: \"ascending\" }, 200, cursor, context);\n   213\t      turns += page.items.filter((entry) => entry.kind === \"pi.assistant\").length;\n   214\t      cursor = page.next;\n   215\t    } while (cursor !== undefined);\n   216\t    return turns;\n   217\t  }\n   218\t\n   219\t  /** Caps the tool rounds of any run of this conversation, so one run cannot overshoot the session's turn budget. */\n   220\t  async limitTurns(id: number, maxTurns: number): Promise<void> {\n   221\t    await (await this.#conversation(id)).configure({ maxTurns }, context);\n   222\t  }\n   223\t\n   224\t  /** The stored state of a submission, for the run watcher. */\n   225\t  async submissionState(id: number, requestId: string): Promise<SubmissionState | undefined> {\n   226\t    return this.#storage.submissionByRequest(id as ConversationId, requestId, context);\n   227\t  }\n   228\t\n   229\t  /**\n   230\t   * Durably admits one inbox event. `requestId` is the inbox row id, so a resubmission after a crash returns the\n   231\t   * original submission instead of adding a second turn. A message queues behind a running turn (follow-up); a\n   232\t   * steer joins the running turn after its current tool round, and starts a turn when the session is idle.\n   233\t   */\n   234\t  async submitInput(\n   235\t    id: number,\n   236\t    input: { text: string; requestId: string; steer: boolean },\n   237\t  ): Promise<void> {\n   238\t    const conversation = await this.#conversation(id);\n   239\t    await conversation.submit(\n   240\t      {\n   241\t        type: \"input\",\n   242\t        content: input.text,\n   243\t        requestId: input.requestId,\n   244\t        whenBusy: input.steer ? \"steer\" : \"followUp\",\n   245\t      },\n   246\t      context,\n   247\t    );\n   248\t  }\n   249\t\n   250\t  async hasSubmission(id: number, requestId: string): Promise<boolean> {\n   251\t    // A read on the Storage: the Harness has no lookup by request id. Only the test-fault gate uses it.\n   252\t    const record = await this.#storage.submissionByRequest(\n   253\t      id as ConversationId,\n   254\t      requestId,\n   255\t      context,\n   256\t    );\n   257\t    return record !== undefined;\n   258\t  }\n   259\t\n   260\t  /** Withdraws queued inputs, aborts the running turn and resolves once the conversation is idle. */\n   261\t  async abort(id: number): Promise<void> {\n   262\t    await (await this.#conversation(id)).abort(context);\n   263\t  }\n   264\t\n   265\t  /** The conversation and a watch of its structural view (a window over the transcript plus live state). */\n   266\t  async watch(\n   267\t    id: number,\n   268\t    window?: ConversationWindow,\n   269\t  ): Promise<{ conversation: Conversation; watch: ConversationWatch } | undefined> {\n   270\t    const conversation = await this.#harness.conversation(id as ConversationId, context);\n   271\t    if (conversation === undefined) return undefined;\n   272\t    return { conversation, watch: await conversation.watch(context, window) };\n   273\t  }\n   274\t\n   275\t  /**\n   276\t   * The session's sandbox env, opening it (claim, bridge) if needed. Only repo sessions call this directly, to clone\n   277\t   * before the first turn; every other session opens its sandbox lazily at the first tool call.\n   278\t   */\n   279\t  async workspaceEnv(id: number): Promise<WorkspaceEnv> {\n   280\t    return (await this.#sandboxes.ensure(id)).env;\n   281\t  }\n   282\t\n   283\t  /** Stops the session's bridge and deletes its SandboxClaim and PVC. */\n   284\t  async destroySandbox(id: number): Promise<void> {\n   285\t    await this.#sandboxes.destroy(id);\n   286\t  }\n   287\t\n   288\t  /** The orphan sweep's delete of a claim and its PVC: the session deletion's teardown, for a claim with no live session. */\n   289\t  async destroyOrphanSandbox(claimName: string, sessionLabel: string): Promise<void> {\n   290\t    await this.#sandboxes.destroyOrphan(claimName, sessionLabel);\n   291\t  }\n   292\t\n   293\t  async #conversation(id: number): Promise<Conversation> {\n   294\t    const conversation = await this.#harness.conversation(id as ConversationId, context);\n   295\t    if (conversation === undefined) throw new Error(`conversation ${String(id)} does not exist`);\n   296\t    return conversation;\n   297\t  }\n   298\t\n   299\t  /** Waits for in-flight work to settle and closes storage; bridges stop, claims stay. */\n   300\t  async close(): Promise<void> {\n   301\t    await this.#harness.close(context);\n   302\t    await this.#sandboxes.closeAll();\n   303\t  }\n   304\t}\n==== packages/orchestrator/src/watcher.ts\n     1\timport type { RunOutcome } from \"./failure.js\";\n     2\t\n     3\t/** One input the orchestrator handed to Pi Durable and has not yet seen settled. */\n     4\texport interface Watched {\n     5\t  sessionId: string;\n     6\t  conversationId: number;\n     7\t  /** The inbox row id: the Pi Durable `requestId` of the submission. */\n     8\t  requestId: string;\n     9\t}\n    10\t\n    11\t/** What the storage says about a submission; only the fields the watcher reads. */\n    12\texport type SubmissionState =\n    13\t  | { status: \"queued\" | \"placed\" }\n    14\t  | { status: \"done\" }\n    15\t  | { status: \"unanswered\"; reason: string; detail?: unknown };\n    16\t\n    17\texport interface RunWatcherOptions {\n    18\t  lookup: (conversationId: number, requestId: string) => Promise<SubmissionState | undefined>;\n    19\t  /** A submission ended `unanswered`: the run it belonged to failed or was aborted. Called once per submission. */\n    20\t  onUnanswered: (watched: Watched, outcome: RunOutcome) => Promise<void>;\n    21\t  pollMs?: number;\n    22\t  onError?: (error: unknown) => void;\n    23\t}\n    24\t\n    25\t/**\n    26\t * Notices runs that end without an answer. Pi Durable reports a model error only inside the conversation (the run's\n    27\t * submissions settle `unanswered` with the reason and error text), not to the host, so the orchestrator reads the\n    28\t * submissions it handed over until each is settled. Polling the storage also covers a run that a previous process\n    29\t * started and this one resumed: `add` it again at start and it is picked up the same way.\n    30\t */\n    31\texport class RunWatcher {\n    32\t  readonly #options: RunWatcherOptions;\n    33\t  readonly #pending = new Map<string, Watched>();\n    34\t  #timer: NodeJS.Timeout | undefined;\n    35\t  #polling = false;\n    36\t\n    37\t  constructor(options: RunWatcherOptions) {\n    38\t    this.#options = options;\n    39\t  }\n    40\t\n    41\t  add(watched: Watched): void {\n    42\t    this.#pending.set(`${String(watched.conversationId)}/${watched.requestId}`, watched);\n    43\t    this.#timer ??= setInterval(() => void this.poll(), this.#options.pollMs ?? 2_000);\n    44\t    this.#timer.unref();\n    45\t  }\n    46\t\n    47\t  get size(): number {\n    48\t    return this.#pending.size;\n    49\t  }\n    50\t\n    51\t  stop(): void {\n    52\t    if (this.#timer !== undefined) clearInterval(this.#timer);\n    53\t    this.#timer = undefined;\n    54\t  }\n    55\t\n    56\t  /** One pass over the pending submissions. Exposed so tests need no timers. */\n    57\t  async poll(): Promise<void> {\n    58\t    if (this.#polling) return;\n    59\t    this.#polling = true;\n    60\t    try {\n    61\t      for (const [key, watched] of [...this.#pending]) {\n    62\t        try {\n    63\t          const state = await this.#options.lookup(watched.conversationId, watched.requestId);\n    64\t          if (state === undefined || state.status === \"done\") {\n    65\t            this.#pending.delete(key);\n    66\t          } else if (state.status === \"unanswered\") {\n    67\t            const detail =\n    68\t              typeof state.detail === \"string\"\n    69\t                ? state.detail\n    70\t                : state.detail === undefined\n    71\t                  ? undefined\n    72\t                  : JSON.stringify(state.detail);\n    73\t            await this.#options.onUnanswered(watched, {\n    74\t              reason: state.reason,\n    75\t              ...(detail === undefined ? {} : { detail }),\n    76\t            });\n    77\t            // Only now: a handler that threw leaves the watch in place, so the failure is not lost.\n    78\t            this.#pending.delete(key);\n    79\t          }\n    80\t        } catch (error) {\n    81\t          // Keep it pending: a storage hiccup must not lose the watch, nor crash the orchestrator.\n    82\t          this.#options.onError?.(error);\n    83\t        }\n    84\t      }\n    85\t    } finally {\n    86\t      this.#polling = false;\n    87\t      if (this.#pending.size === 0) this.stop();\n    88\t    }\n    89\t  }\n    90\t}\n==== packages/orchestrator/src/stream.ts\n     1\timport { once } from \"node:events\";\n     2\timport type { IncomingMessage, ServerResponse } from \"node:http\";\n     3\timport { BACKGROUND_CONTEXT as context } from \"@earendil-works/chord/context\";\n     4\timport type { ConversationView, EntryRecord } from \"@earendil-works/pi-durable\";\n     5\timport { errorMessage } from \"@pi-durable-k8s/session-core\";\n     6\timport type { Host } from \"./host.js\";\n     7\timport { toEvent } from \"./host.js\";\n     8\timport { log } from \"./log.js\";\n     9\timport type { StreamRegistry } from \"./sessions.js\";\n    10\t\n    11\tconst KEEPALIVE_MS = 15_000;\n    12\tconst GAP_PAGE = 100;\n    13\t\n    14\t/** What the client sees of the run in progress. Carries no SSE id: it is not addressable by a cursor. */\n    15\texport interface LiveEvent {\n    16\t  running: boolean;\n    17\t  /** Inputs queued behind the running turn. */\n    18\t  queued: number;\n    19\t  /** The throttled partial answer of the response being generated, if any. */\n    20\t  partial?: string;\n    21\t  tools?: { callId: string; name: string; status: string }[];\n    22\t  /** Why the newest run ended without an answer, e.g. `aborted`. */\n    23\t  runFailure?: string;\n    24\t}\n    25\t\n    26\tfunction asObject(value: unknown): Record<string, unknown> | undefined {\n    27\t  return typeof value === \"object\" && value !== null && !Array.isArray(value)\n    28\t    ? (value as Record<string, unknown>)\n    29\t    : undefined;\n    30\t}\n    31\t\n    32\t/** Projects `pi.live` and `pi.inbox` of a conversation view. Defensive: these are plain JSON documents. */\n    33\texport function liveEvent(docs: ConversationView[\"docs\"]): LiveEvent {\n    34\t  const live = asObject(docs[\"pi.live\"]);\n    35\t  const inbox = asObject(docs[\"pi.inbox\"]);\n    36\t  const items = inbox?.items;\n    37\t  const event: LiveEvent = {\n    38\t    running: live?.run !== undefined,\n    39\t    queued: Array.isArray(items) ? items.length : 0,\n    40\t  };\n    41\t  const content = asObject(asObject(live?.generation)?.message)?.content;\n    42\t  if (Array.isArray(content)) {\n    43\t    const partial = content\n    44\t      .map((block) => {\n    45\t        const b = asObject(block);\n    46\t        return b?.type === \"text\" && typeof b.text === \"string\" ? b.text : \"\";\n    47\t      })\n    48\t      .join(\"\");\n    49\t    if (partial !== \"\") event.partial = partial;\n    50\t  }\n    51\t  if (Array.isArray(live?.tools)) {\n    52\t    event.tools = (live.tools as unknown[]).flatMap((slot) => {\n    53\t      const s = asObject(slot);\n    54\t      return s !== undefined\n    55\t        ? [{ callId: String(s.callId), name: String(s.name), status: String(s.status) }]\n    56\t        : [];\n    57\t    });\n    58\t  }\n    59\t  const failure = asObject(live?.runFailure);\n    60\t  if (typeof failure?.reason === \"string\") event.runFailure = failure.reason;\n    61\t  return event;\n    62\t}\n    63\t\n    64\t/** Only entries that carry model messages are streamed (inputs, answers, tool calls and results). */\n    65\tfunction entryEvent(\n    66\t  entry: EntryRecord,\n    67\t): { id: number; kind: string; messages: unknown[] } | undefined {\n    68\t  // System messages (the rendered system prompt) are the host's, not the conversation's: never streamed.\n    69\t  const messages = (entry.model ?? []).filter((message) => message.role !== \"system\");\n    70\t  if (messages.length === 0) return undefined;\n    71\t  return { id: entry.id, kind: entry.kind, messages: messages.map(toEvent) };\n    72\t}\n    73\t\n    74\texport function parseLastEventId(header: string | string[] | undefined): number {\n    75\t  const raw = Array.isArray(header) ? header[0] : header;\n    76\t  const value = Number(raw);\n    77\t  return raw !== undefined && Number.isSafeInteger(value) && value > 0 ? value : 0;\n    78\t}\n    79\t\n    80\t/** Writes a chunk and waits for the socket to drain, or for the client to go away. */\n    81\tasync function write(res: ServerResponse, chunk: string): Promise<void> {\n    82\t  if (res.destroyed || res.writableEnded) return;\n    83\t  if (!res.write(chunk)) {\n    84\t    await Promise.race([once(res, \"drain\"), once(res, \"close\")]).catch(() => undefined);\n    85\t  }\n    86\t}\n    87\t\n    88\t/**\n    89\t * Server-sent events for one conversation, built on `Conversation.watch()` (the conversation view).\n    90\t *\n    91\t *  - `event: entry`, `id: <entry id>`: a committed transcript entry, once, in order. The id is the cursor.\n    92\t *  - `event: live`, no id: the run in progress (partial answer, tool calls, queue). Sent whole on connect and\n    93\t *    on every change; not replayed from a cursor, so a reconnect starts from the current state of the response.\n    94\t *  - `event: deleted`: the session was deleted; the stream ends.\n    95\t *\n    96\t * A client reconnects with `Last-Event-ID: <last entry id>`: entries after it are sent first (those the\n    97\t * watch's window no longer holds are read with `Conversation.entries()`), then live updates. Without the\n    98\t * header the whole transcript is replayed from the start.\n    99\t */\n   100\texport async function serveStream(\n   101\t  req: IncomingMessage,\n   102\t  res: ServerResponse,\n   103\t  host: Host,\n   104\t  streams: StreamRegistry,\n   105\t  sessionId: string,\n   106\t  conversationId: number,\n   107\t): Promise<void> {\n   108\t  const watched = await host.watch(conversationId);\n   109\t  if (watched === undefined) {\n   110\t    res.writeHead(404, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" });\n   111\t    res.end(JSON.stringify({ error: \"conversation not found\" }));\n   112\t    return;\n   113\t  }\n   114\t  const { conversation, watch } = watched;\n   115\t  let cursor = parseLastEventId(req.headers[\"last-event-id\"]);\n   116\t\n   117\t  res.writeHead(200, {\n   118\t    \"content-type\": \"text/event-stream\",\n   119\t    \"cache-control\": \"no-cache\",\n   120\t    connection: \"keep-alive\",\n   121\t    \"x-accel-buffering\": \"no\",\n   122\t  });\n   123\t  res.write(\"retry: 2000\\n\\n\");\n   124\t\n   125\t  let lastLive = \"\";\n   126\t  const finish = (reason?: string): void => {\n   127\t    clearInterval(keepalive);\n   128\t    unregister();\n   129\t    void watch.stop();\n   130\t    if (res.writableEnded || res.destroyed) return;\n   131\t    if (reason !== undefined) res.write(`event: ${reason}\\ndata: {}\\n\\n`);\n   132\t    res.end();\n   133\t  };\n   134\t  const keepalive = setInterval(() => {\n   135\t    if (!res.destroyed) res.write(\": keepalive\\n\\n\");\n   136\t  }, KEEPALIVE_MS);\n   137\t  const unregister = streams.add(sessionId, finish);\n   138\t  res.on(\"close\", () => finish());\n   139\t\n   140\t  const sendEntry = async (entry: EntryRecord): Promise<void> => {\n   141\t    if (entry.id <= cursor) return;\n   142\t    cursor = entry.id;\n   143\t    const event = entryEvent(entry);\n   144\t    if (event !== undefined) {\n   145\t      await write(res, `id: ${String(event.id)}\\nevent: entry\\ndata: ${JSON.stringify(event)}\\n\\n`);\n   146\t    }\n   147\t  };\n   148\t\n   149\t  const emit = async (view: ConversationView): Promise<void> => {\n   150\t    // The window may start after the client's cursor (long outage, or a fresh connect): read the gap.\n   151\t    if (view.before !== undefined && view.before > cursor) {\n   152\t      let after = cursor;\n   153\t      for (;;) {\n   154\t        const page = await conversation.entries(\n   155\t          {\n   156\t            minEntryId: (after + 1) as EntryRecord[\"id\"],\n   157\t            maxEntryId: view.before,\n   158\t            order: \"ascending\",\n   159\t          },\n   160\t          GAP_PAGE,\n   161\t          undefined,\n   162\t          context,\n   163\t        );\n   164\t        for (const entry of page.items) await sendEntry(entry);\n   165\t        const newest = page.items.at(-1);\n   166\t        if (newest === undefined || page.items.length < GAP_PAGE) break;\n   167\t        after = newest.id;\n   168\t      }\n   169\t    }\n   170\t    for (const entry of view.entries) await sendEntry(entry);\n   171\t    const live = JSON.stringify(liveEvent(view.docs));\n   172\t    if (live !== lastLive) {\n   173\t      lastLive = live;\n   174\t      await write(res, `event: live\\ndata: ${live}\\n\\n`);\n   175\t    }\n   176\t  };\n   177\t\n   178\t  try {\n   179\t    await emit(watch.value);\n   180\t  } catch (error) {\n   181\t    log(\"stream-failed\", { session: sessionId, message: errorMessage(error) });\n   182\t    finish();\n   183\t    return;\n   184\t  }\n   185\t  watch.start(async (call) => {\n   186\t    if (call.kind !== \"value\") return;\n   187\t    await emit(call.value);\n   188\t  });\n   189\t  // The watch ends when the Harness closes (orchestrator shutdown) or fails: end the response so the client reconnects.\n   190\t  void watch.closed.then(() => {\n   191\t    finish();\n   192\t  });\n   193\t}\n==== packages/orchestrator/src/main.ts\n     1\timport {\n     2\t  applyMigrations,\n     3\t  conversationsWithExecInFlight,\n     4\t  createPool,\n     5\t  errorMessage,\n     6\t  getSession,\n     7\t  listSessionRefs,\n     8\t  setExecInFlight,\n     9\t  tokenAuthenticator,\n    10\t} from \"@pi-durable-k8s/session-core\";\n    11\timport { loadConfig } from \"./config.js\";\n    12\timport type { FetchLike } from \"./github-app.js\";\n    13\timport { OneCliAdmin } from \"./onecli-admin.js\";\n    14\timport { RepoAccess } from \"./repo-access.js\";\n    15\timport type { SandboxHooks } from \"./sandboxes.js\";\n    16\timport { Host } from \"./host.js\";\n    17\timport { createOrchestratorServer } from \"./http.js\";\n    18\timport type { Lifecycle } from \"./http.js\";\n    19\timport { InboxLoop } from \"./inbox.js\";\n    20\timport { listClaims, listPvcs } from \"./kube.js\";\n    21\timport { log } from \"./log.js\";\n    22\timport { SessionService } from \"./sessions.js\";\n    23\timport { openStorageWhenFree } from \"./storage.js\";\n    24\timport { OrphanSweeper } from \"./sweeper.js\";\n    25\t\n    26\tasync function main(): Promise<void> {\n    27\t  const config = loadConfig(process.env);\n    28\t  const lifecycle: Lifecycle = { state: \"waiting-for-lock\", instance: config.instance };\n    29\t  // A second, independent connection pool for the inbox and the owner check: the Pi Durable adapter pins its\n    30\t  // own connection and holds the ownership lock on it, and neither may share it.\n    31\t  const pool = createPool(config.databaseUrl, `${config.instance}-inbox`, 10);\n    32\t  const server = createOrchestratorServer({\n    33\t    lifecycle,\n    34\t    authenticate: tokenAuthenticator(config.apiTokens),\n    35\t    pool,\n    36\t    control: config.control,\n    37\t  });\n    38\t  await new Promise<void>((resolve) => server.listen(config.port, resolve));\n    39\t  log(\"listening\", { instance: config.instance, port: config.port });\n    40\t\n    41\t  const running: { inbox?: InboxLoop; service?: SessionService; sweeper?: OrphanSweeper } = {};\n    42\t  const stop = new AbortController();\n    43\t  const shutdown = (signal: string): void => {\n    44\t    log(\"shutdown\", { signal });\n    45\t    stop.abort();\n    46\t    server.close();\n    47\t    void (async () => {\n    48\t      running.service?.stop();\n    49\t      running.sweeper?.stop();\n    50\t      await running.inbox?.stop();\n    51\t      await lifecycle.host?.close();\n    52\t      server.closeAllConnections();\n    53\t      await pool.end().catch(() => undefined);\n    54\t    })().finally(() => process.exit(0));\n    55\t    setTimeout(() => process.exit(0), 10_000).unref();\n    56\t  };\n    57\t  process.on(\"SIGTERM\", () => shutdown(\"SIGTERM\"));\n    58\t  process.on(\"SIGINT\", () => shutdown(\"SIGINT\"));\n    59\t\n    60\t  for (;;) {\n    61\t    try {\n    62\t      await applyMigrations(pool);\n    63\t      break;\n    64\t    } catch (error) {\n    65\t      log(\"migrate-failed\", { message: errorMessage(error) });\n    66\t      await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 2_000));\n    67\t    }\n    68\t  }\n    69\t\n    70\t  const storage = await openStorageWhenFree(config, stop.signal);\n    71\t  log(\"lock-acquired\", { instance: config.instance });\n    72\t  const sessionKeyOf = async (conversationId: number): Promise<string> => {\n    73\t    const { rows } = await pool.query<{ id: string }>(\n    74\t      \"select id from inbox.sessions where conversation_id = $1\",\n    75\t      [conversationId],\n    76\t    );\n    77\t    // Conversations the inbox does not know are the test-only /control sessions.\n    78\t    return rows[0]?.id ?? `control-${String(conversationId)}`;\n    79\t  };\n    80\t  // Repo workspaces (Phase 4c). Plain sessions never touch OneCLI's management API or GitHub through this.\n    81\t  const callApi: FetchLike = (url, init) => fetch(url, init);\n    82\t  const onecli =\n    83\t    config.repos.onecliApiKey === undefined\n    84\t      ? undefined\n    85\t      : new OneCliAdmin(config.repos.onecliApi, config.repos.onecliApiKey, callApi);\n    86\t  const repos = new RepoAccess({\n    87\t    pool,\n    88\t    onecli,\n    89\t    githubAppDir: config.repos.githubAppDir,\n    90\t    gateway: config.onecli.gateway,\n    91\t    caFile: config.onecli.caFile,\n    92\t    fetch: callApi,\n    93\t  });\n    94\t  const hooks: SandboxHooks = {\n    95\t    shellEnv: async (conversationId) => {\n    96\t      const { rows } = await pool.query<{ id: string }>(\n    97\t        \"select id from inbox.sessions where conversation_id = $1\",\n    98\t        [conversationId],\n    99\t      );\n   100\t      const session = rows[0] === undefined ? undefined : await getSession(pool, rows[0].id);\n   101\t      return session === undefined ? undefined : repos.shellEnv(session, conversationId);\n   102\t    },\n   103\t    beforeUse: (conversationId) => repos.beforeUse(conversationId),\n   104\t    execInFlight: (conversationId, inFlight) => setExecInFlight(pool, conversationId, inFlight),\n   105\t  };\n   106\t  // Sandboxes that had a command running when the previous process died: Host.open recycles their Pods before Pi\n   107\t  // Durable resumes (docs/decisions/0003-recycle-pod-on-interrupt.md).\n   108\t  const recycleAtStart = await conversationsWithExecInFlight(pool);\n   109\t  if (recycleAtStart.length > 0) log(\"recycle-at-start\", { conversations: recycleAtStart });\n   110\t  const host = await Host.open(\n   111\t    storage,\n   112\t    config,\n   113\t    (error) => {\n   114\t      // Fail closed: a Harness that lost its storage stops here. Nothing reconnects and nothing more is\n   115\t      // written; the Deployment starts a fresh process, which waits for the lock like any other owner.\n   116\t      log(\"fail-closed\", { instance: config.instance, message: errorMessage(error) });\n   117\t      process.exit(1);\n   118\t    },\n   119\t    sessionKeyOf,\n   120\t    hooks,\n   121\t    recycleAtStart,\n   122\t  );\n   123\t  const service = new SessionService(pool, host, {\n   124\t    testFaults: config.testFaults,\n   125\t    defaultModel: config.models.default,\n   126\t    turnBudget: config.turnBudget,\n   127\t    repos,\n   128\t  });\n   129\t  running.service = service;\n   130\t  // Not fatal: a failed scan only means a run that died unseen is noticed at its next input.\n   131\t  await service.recoverWatches().catch((error: unknown) => {\n   132\t    log(\"run-watch-recover-failed\", { message: errorMessage(error) });\n   133\t  });\n   134\t  lifecycle.host = host;\n   135\t  lifecycle.service = service;\n   136\t  lifecycle.state = \"owner\";\n   137\t  log(\"owner\", { instance: config.instance });\n   138\t\n   139\t  // Orphan sweep (docs/decisions/0002-orphan-sweep.md): only the owner runs it, like the inbox.\n   140\t  const sweeper = new OrphanSweeper({\n   141\t    listSessions: () => listSessionRefs(pool),\n   142\t    listClaims: () => listClaims(config.namespace),\n   143\t    listPvcs: () => listPvcs(config.namespace),\n   144\t    listOneCli:\n   145\t      onecli === undefined\n   146\t        ? undefined\n   147\t        : async () => ({\n   148\t            agents: (await onecli.listAgents()).map(({ id, identifier }) => ({ id, identifier })),\n   149\t            secrets: await onecli.listSecrets(),\n   150\t          }),\n   151\t    destroyClaim: (claim, label) => host.destroyOrphanSandbox(claim, label),\n   152\t    revokeSession: (sessionId) => repos.revokeSession(sessionId),\n   153\t    graceMs: config.sweep.graceMs,\n   154\t    maxActions: config.sweep.maxActions,\n   155\t  });\n   156\t  running.sweeper = sweeper;\n   157\t  sweeper.start(config.sweep.intervalMs);\n   158\t\n   159\t  // Only the owner consumes the inbox. Rows that arrived while no orchestrator ran are waiting.\n   160\t  const inbox = new InboxLoop(pool, (event, session) => service.apply(event, session));\n   161\t  running.inbox = inbox;\n   162\t  inbox.start();\n   163\t}\n   164\t\n   165\tmain().catch((error: unknown) => {\n   166\t  log(\"fatal\", { message: errorMessage(error) });\n   167\t  process.exit(1);\n   168\t});\n==== packages/orchestrator/src/failure.ts\n     1\t/** What a run that ended without an answer means for the session (Pi Durable `RunFailure`, plus the text of the error). */\n     2\texport interface RunOutcome {\n     3\t  reason: string;\n     4\t  detail?: string;\n     5\t}\n     6\t\n     7\t/**\n     8\t * Model-side signs that the credentials are not accepted: an HTTP status of 401 or 403 from the provider (a missing\n     9\t * or revoked key, a revoked OneCLI grant leaves the gateway injecting nothing), 407 from the gateway itself (the\n    10\t * agent token was deleted or regenerated), the gateway's own answer when the agent has no grant for the host (a 401\n    11\t * whose JSON body, which is all pi-ai keeps, reads `access_restricted` / `this agent does not have access`), or the\n    12\t * usual wording. Status codes must stand alone, so a request id or a\n    13\t * byte count that happens to contain 401 does not match.\n    14\t */\n    15\tconst REJECTED =\n    16\t  /(?<![a-z0-9])(?:401|403|407)(?![a-z0-9])|unauthori[sz]ed|forbidden|invalid[ _-]?api[ _-]?key|incorrect api key|proxy authentication|authentication[ _-]?(?:error|failed)|permission[ _-]?denied|access_restricted|does not have access/i;\n    17\t\n    18\t/**\n    19\t * The terminal failure a run outcome maps to, or undefined when the session stays usable.\n    20\t *  - A model error that reads as rejected credentials is terminal: nothing in the orchestrator can fix a grant, and\n    21\t *    retrying only repeats paid or rate-limited calls. (pi-ai does not retry these statuses either.)\n    22\t *  - `turn_limit` is the per-session turn budget (`maxTurns`).\n    23\t *  - Everything else (a 429 that outlasted the retries, a network error, an abort) leaves the session active: the\n    24\t *    next message starts a new run.\n    25\t */\n    26\texport function terminalFailure(outcome: RunOutcome): string | undefined {\n    27\t  if (outcome.reason === \"turn_limit\") {\n    28\t    return \"turn budget exhausted: the session used all the model turns it is allowed\";\n    29\t  }\n    30\t  if (outcome.reason === \"model_error\" && REJECTED.test(outcome.detail ?? \"\")) {\n    31\t    return \"model credentials were rejected (401/403): the OneCLI agent token or its grant for this provider is missing or revoked\";\n    32\t  }\n    33\t  return undefined;\n    34\t}\n==== packages/session-core/src/store.ts\n     1\timport { randomUUID } from \"node:crypto\";\n     2\timport type pg from \"pg\";\n     3\timport { THINKING_LEVELS } from \"./models.js\";\n     4\timport type { ModelChoice } from \"./models.js\";\n     5\timport type { RepoSpec } from \"./repo.js\";\n     6\t\n     7\t/** `failed` is terminal: the model credentials were rejected or the turn budget is used up. Only DELETE is accepted. */\n     8\texport type SessionStatus = \"active\" | \"deleting\" | \"deleted\" | \"failed\";\n     9\texport type EventKind = \"message\" | \"steer\" | \"cancel\" | \"delete\";\n    10\texport type EventStatus = \"pending\" | \"submitted\" | \"failed\";\n    11\t\n    12\texport interface SessionRow {\n    13\t  id: string;\n    14\t  owner: string;\n    15\t  /** Subject of the creating principal; the owner check compares this, not `owner`. */\n    16\t  ownerSubject: string | null;\n    17\t  status: SessionStatus;\n    18\t  /** Pi Durable conversation id; null until the orchestrator has created it. */\n    19\t  conversationId: number | null;\n    20\t  /** The model chosen at creation; null for sessions that predate migration 002 (they run the default). */\n    21\t  model: ModelChoice | null;\n    22\t  /** Why the session is `failed`; null otherwise. */\n    23\t  failure: string | null;\n    24\t  /** The repository workspace asked for at creation; null for a plain session (no OneCLI objects exist). */\n    25\t  repo: RepoSpec | null;\n    26\t  /** OneCLI agent and secret ids of a repo session, once provisioned. Ids only, never values. */\n    27\t  onecli: { agentId: string; secretIds: string[] } | null;\n    28\t  /** When the clone and the workspace marker were first completed; null before. */\n    29\t  workspaceReadyAt: Date | null;\n    30\t  createdAt: Date;\n    31\t  lastActivityAt: Date;\n    32\t}\n    33\t\n    34\texport interface InboxEvent {\n    35\t  /** bigint, so a string. Also the Pi Durable `requestId` of the submission. */\n    36\t  id: string;\n    37\t  sessionId: string;\n    38\t  source: string;\n    39\t  sourceEventId: string;\n    40\t  kind: EventKind;\n    41\t  payload: { text?: string; [key: string]: unknown };\n    42\t  status: EventStatus;\n    43\t  attempts: number;\n    44\t  createdAt: Date;\n    45\t  submittedAt: Date | null;\n    46\t  error: string | null;\n    47\t}\n    48\t\n    49\tinterface SessionDbRow {\n    50\t  id: string;\n    51\t  owner: string;\n    52\t  owner_subject: string | null;\n    53\t  status: SessionStatus;\n    54\t  conversation_id: string | null;\n    55\t  model_provider: string | null;\n    56\t  model_id: string | null;\n    57\t  model_reasoning: string | null;\n    58\t  failure: string | null;\n    59\t  repo: string | null;\n    60\t  repo_branch: string | null;\n    61\t  onecli_agent_id: string | null;\n    62\t  onecli_secret_ids: string[] | null;\n    63\t  workspace_ready_at: Date | null;\n    64\t  created_at: Date;\n    65\t  last_activity_at: Date;\n    66\t}\n    67\t\n    68\texport interface EventDbRow {\n    69\t  id: string;\n    70\t  session_id: string;\n    71\t  source: string;\n    72\t  source_event_id: string;\n    73\t  kind: EventKind;\n    74\t  payload: InboxEvent[\"payload\"];\n    75\t  status: EventStatus;\n    76\t  attempts: number;\n    77\t  created_at: Date;\n    78\t  submitted_at: Date | null;\n    79\t  error: string | null;\n    80\t}\n    81\t\n    82\tconst toSession = (row: SessionDbRow): SessionRow => ({\n    83\t  id: row.id,\n    84\t  owner: row.owner,\n    85\t  ownerSubject: row.owner_subject,\n    86\t  status: row.status,\n    87\t  conversationId: row.conversation_id === null ? null : Number(row.conversation_id),\n    88\t  model:\n    89\t    row.model_provider === null || row.model_id === null\n    90\t      ? null\n    91\t      : {\n    92\t          provider: row.model_provider,\n    93\t          model: row.model_id,\n    94\t          ...reasoningOf(row.model_reasoning),\n    95\t        },\n    96\t  failure: row.failure,\n    97\t  repo:\n    98\t    row.repo === null\n    99\t      ? null\n   100\t      : { repo: row.repo, ...(row.repo_branch === null ? {} : { branch: row.repo_branch }) },\n   101\t  onecli:\n   102\t    row.onecli_agent_id === null\n   103\t      ? null\n   104\t      : { agentId: row.onecli_agent_id, secretIds: row.onecli_secret_ids ?? [] },\n   105\t  workspaceReadyAt: row.workspace_ready_at,\n   106\t  createdAt: row.created_at,\n   107\t  lastActivityAt: row.last_activity_at,\n   108\t});\n   109\t\n   110\tfunction reasoningOf(value: string | null): Pick<ModelChoice, \"reasoning\"> {\n   111\t  const level = THINKING_LEVELS.find((candidate) => candidate === value);\n   112\t  return level === undefined ? {} : { reasoning: level };\n   113\t}\n   114\t\n   115\texport const toEvent = (row: EventDbRow): InboxEvent => ({\n   116\t  id: row.id,\n   117\t  sessionId: row.session_id,\n   118\t  source: row.source,\n   119\t  sourceEventId: row.source_event_id,\n   120\t  kind: row.kind,\n   121\t  payload: row.payload,\n   122\t  status: row.status,\n   123\t  attempts: row.attempts,\n   124\t  createdAt: row.created_at,\n   125\t  submittedAt: row.submitted_at,\n   126\t  error: row.error,\n   127\t});\n   128\t\n   129\t/** Session ids are random UUIDs (v4), never sequential: an id cannot be guessed from another. */\n   130\texport async function createSession(\n   131\t  pool: pg.Pool,\n   132\t  principal: { owner: string; subject: string },\n   133\t  model: ModelChoice,\n   134\t  repo?: RepoSpec,\n   135\t): Promise<string> {\n   136\t  const id = randomUUID();\n   137\t  await pool.query(\n   138\t    \"insert into inbox.sessions (id, owner, owner_subject, model_provider, model_id, model_reasoning, repo, repo_branch) values ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5, $6, $7, $8)\",\n   139\t    [\n   140\t      id,\n   141\t      principal.owner,\n   142\t      principal.subject,\n   143\t      model.provider,\n   144\t      model.model,\n   145\t      model.reasoning ?? null,\n   146\t      repo?.repo ?? null,\n   147\t      repo?.branch ?? null,\n   148\t    ],\n   149\t  );\n   150\t  return id;\n   151\t}\n   152\t\n   153\t/** Moves an active session to the terminal `failed` state. False if it was not active (failed already, deleting, deleted). */\n   154\texport async function failSession(\n   155\t  db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">,\n   156\t  sessionId: string,\n   157\t  failure: string,\n   158\t): Promise<boolean> {\n   159\t  const result = await db.query(\n   160\t    `update inbox.sessions set status = 'failed', failure = $2, last_activity_at = clock_timestamp()\n   161\t      where id = $1 and status = 'active'`,\n   162\t    [sessionId, failure.slice(0, 500)],\n   163\t  );\n   164\t  return (result.rowCount ?? 0) > 0;\n   165\t}\n   166\t\n   167\texport async function getSession(\n   168\t  db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">,\n   169\t  id: string,\n   170\t): Promise<SessionRow | undefined> {\n   171\t  const { rows } = await db.query<SessionDbRow>(\"select * from inbox.sessions where id = $1\", [id]);\n   172\t  const row = rows[0];\n   173\t  return row === undefined ? undefined : toSession(row);\n   174\t}\n   175\t\n   176\texport type EnqueueResult =\n   177\t  | { outcome: \"accepted\"; eventId: string }\n   178\t  /** The same (source, source_event_id) was already stored: nothing new was written. */\n   179\t  | { outcome: \"duplicate\"; eventId: string }\n   180\t  /** The (source, source_event_id) belongs to another session. */\n   181\t  | { outcome: \"conflict\" };\n   182\t\n   183\t/**\n   184\t * Writes one event and returns. The unique index on (source, source_event_id) makes a repeated post a no-op that\n   185\t * returns the first event's id. The orchestrator is not involved: this works while it is down.\n   186\t */\n   187\texport async function enqueueEvent(\n   188\t  pool: pg.Pool,\n   189\t  event: {\n   190\t    sessionId: string;\n   191\t    source: string;\n   192\t    sourceEventId: string;\n   193\t    kind: EventKind;\n   194\t    payload: InboxEvent[\"payload\"];\n   195\t  },\n   196\t): Promise<EnqueueResult> {\n   197\t  const inserted = await pool.query<{ id: string }>(\n   198\t    `insert into inbox.events (session_id, source, source_event_id, kind, payload)\n   199\t     values ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5)\n   200\t     on conflict (source, source_event_id) do nothing\n   201\t     returning id`,\n   202\t    [event.sessionId, event.source, event.sourceEventId, event.kind, JSON.stringify(event.payload)],\n   203\t  );\n   204\t  const fresh = inserted.rows[0];\n   205\t  if (fresh !== undefined) {\n   206\t    await pool.query(\n   207\t      \"update inbox.sessions set last_activity_at = clock_timestamp() where id = $1\",\n   208\t      [event.sessionId],\n   209\t    );\n   210\t    return { outcome: \"accepted\", eventId: fresh.id };\n   211\t  }\n   212\t  const { rows } = await pool.query<{ id: string; session_id: string }>(\n   213\t    \"select id, session_id from inbox.events where source = $1 and source_event_id = $2\",\n   214\t    [event.source, event.sourceEventId],\n   215\t  );\n   216\t  const existing = rows[0];\n   217\t  if (existing === undefined || existing.session_id !== event.sessionId) {\n   218\t    return { outcome: \"conflict\" };\n   219\t  }\n   220\t  return { outcome: \"duplicate\", eventId: existing.id };\n   221\t}\n   222\t\n   223\t/** Marks an active session as being deleted, so no further events are accepted. Idempotent. */\n   224\texport async function requestDelete(pool: pg.Pool, sessionId: string): Promise<void> {\n   225\t  await pool.query(\n   226\t    \"update inbox.sessions set status = 'deleting', last_activity_at = clock_timestamp() where id = $1 and status in ('active', 'failed')\",\n   227\t    [sessionId],\n   228\t  );\n   229\t}\n   230\t\n   231\texport interface SessionSummary {\n   232\t  status: SessionStatus;\n   233\t  lastActivityAt: Date;\n   234\t  events: Record<EventStatus, number>;\n   235\t}\n   236\t\n   237\texport async function summarize(pool: pg.Pool, session: SessionRow): Promise<SessionSummary> {\n   238\t  const { rows } = await pool.query<{ status: EventStatus; n: string }>(\n   239\t    \"select status, count(*) as n from inbox.events where session_id = $1 group by status\",\n   240\t    [session.id],\n   241\t  );\n   242\t  const events: Record<EventStatus, number> = { pending: 0, submitted: 0, failed: 0 };\n   243\t  for (const row of rows) events[row.status] = Number(row.n);\n   244\t  return { status: session.status, lastActivityAt: session.lastActivityAt, events };\n   245\t}\n   246\t\n   247\t/** Records the OneCLI objects of a repo session. Ids only: no token or secret value is ever stored here. */\n   248\texport async function setOneCliObjects(\n   249\t  db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">,\n   250\t  sessionId: string,\n   251\t  agentId: string,\n   252\t  secretIds: readonly string[],\n   253\t): Promise<void> {\n   254\t  await db.query(\n   255\t    \"update inbox.sessions set onecli_agent_id = $2, onecli_secret_ids = $3 where id = $1\",\n   256\t    [sessionId, agentId, [...secretIds]],\n   257\t  );\n   258\t}\n   259\t\n   260\t/** Marks the repo workspace as cloned. Keeps the first time if called again. */\n   261\texport async function markWorkspaceReady(\n   262\t  db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">,\n   263\t  sessionId: string,\n   264\t): Promise<void> {\n   265\t  await db.query(\n   266\t    \"update inbox.sessions set workspace_ready_at = coalesce(workspace_ready_at, clock_timestamp()) where id = $1\",\n   267\t    [sessionId],\n   268\t  );\n   269\t}\n   270\t\n   271\t/**\n   272\t * First step of session deletion: records what the session held, so a crash before the OneCLI objects and the claim\n   273\t * are gone still leaves the list of what to revoke. Safe to repeat; the first record stays.\n   274\t */\n   275\texport async function writeTombstone(\n   276\t  db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">,\n   277\t  session: SessionRow,\n   278\t): Promise<void> {\n   279\t  await db.query(\n   280\t    `insert into inbox.tombstones (session_id, conversation_id, repo, onecli_agent_id, onecli_secret_ids)\n   281\t     values ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5)\n   282\t     on conflict (session_id) do nothing`,\n   283\t    [\n   284\t      session.id,\n   285\t      session.conversationId,\n   286\t      session.repo?.repo ?? null,\n   287\t      session.onecli?.agentId ?? null,\n   288\t      session.onecli === null ? null : [...session.onecli.secretIds],\n   289\t    ],\n   290\t  );\n   291\t}\n   292\t\n   293\texport async function completeTombstone(\n   294\t  db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">,\n   295\t  sessionId: string,\n   296\t): Promise<void> {\n   297\t  await db.query(\n   298\t    \"update inbox.tombstones set completed_at = coalesce(completed_at, clock_timestamp()) where session_id = $1\",\n   299\t    [sessionId],\n   300\t  );\n   301\t}\n   302\t\n   303\t/**\n   304\t * Records that a command may be running (or was interrupted) in the sandbox of this conversation. Called when a\n   305\t * burst of commands starts; a process that dies mid-command never clears it, which is the signal to recycle the Pod.\n   306\t * A conversation without a session row (the test-only control sessions) updates nothing.\n   307\t */\n   308\texport async function setExecInFlight(\n   309\t  db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">,\n   310\t  conversationId: number,\n   311\t  inFlight: boolean,\n   312\t): Promise<void> {\n   313\t  await db.query(\n   314\t    \"update inbox.sessions set exec_in_flight_at = case when $2::boolean then clock_timestamp() else null end where conversation_id = $1\",\n   315\t    [conversationId, inFlight],\n   316\t  );\n   317\t}\n   318\t\n   319\t/** Conversations whose sandbox had a command in flight when the last orchestrator process stopped. */\n   320\texport async function conversationsWithExecInFlight(db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">): Promise<number[]> {\n   321\t  const { rows } = await db.query<{ conversation_id: string }>(\n   322\t    \"select conversation_id from inbox.sessions where exec_in_flight_at is not null and conversation_id is not null and status in ('active', 'failed', 'deleting')\",\n   323\t  );\n   324\t  return rows.map((row) => Number(row.conversation_id));\n   325\t}\n   326\t\n   327\t/** What the orphan sweep needs to know about every session: no owner, model or repo. */\n   328\texport interface SessionRef {\n   329\t  id: string;\n   330\t  status: SessionStatus;\n   331\t  conversationId: number | null;\n   332\t}\n   333\t\n   334\texport async function listSessionRefs(db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">): Promise<SessionRef[]> {\n   335\t  const { rows } = await db.query<{\n   336\t    id: string;\n   337\t    status: SessionStatus;\n   338\t    conversation_id: string | null;\n   339\t  }>(\"select id, status, conversation_id from inbox.sessions\");\n   340\t  return rows.map((row) => ({\n   341\t    id: row.id,\n   342\t    status: row.status,\n   343\t    conversationId: row.conversation_id === null ? null : Number(row.conversation_id),\n   344\t  }));\n   345\t}\n<harness>\n[info] Full output: /tmp/tmp-kLbCeN/pi-output-b03feac7-5c74-44f0-8088-ce0cc582004b.log\n[warn] Output truncated to its end: 198 lines, 8709 bytes dropped\n</harness>","isError":false}]}
